<div id="2026-09-26-root-config-public-exposure" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-26 — Security: root/config/* no longer publicly downloadable</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Files under <code>root/config/</code> (including <code>worktrees.json</code>, <code>ai_kill_switch.json</code>, <code>api/cloudflare_config.json</code> (with api_token placeholder), coa_templates/*.json, gifi_codes.json, services.json, ai_usage.json and similar) were served directly by Static::Simple for any unauthenticated requester at paths like <code>/config/worktrees.json</code>. (Example given by reporter: ai_grounding.json class of files; no exact file of that name found, but the exposure class was real.)</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> <code>Plugin::Static::Simple</code> was configured with <code>include_path =&gt; ['root']</code> (and dirs limited to static/Legacy). This made the entire root/ tree (minus some dirs) web-accessible without login or controller checks. Leaked internal branch/port map, AI kill-switch, accounting structures, and credential references. Confirmed via code inspection of Comserv.pm and directory contents; live HTTP verification blocked by pre-existing :3001 responsiveness issue (backlog + worker state, independent of this).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix.</strong> Changed static configuration to serve only from explicit public directories (<code>root/static</code>, <code>root/LegacyStaticPages</code>) and added <code>ignore =&gt; [ qr{^config/} ]</code>. Private config remains loadable by Perl code via filesystem paths (unchanged).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv.pm</code></p>
</div>
